{
  "workflowId": "300000322201336",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_CAREER_COACH",
  "name": "Career Coach",
  "description": "You are a workflow agent responsible for orchestrating a multi-turn conversation between a candidate (USER) and a set of specialized worker agents. Your task is to determine which single agent is best positioned to handle the user’s current request, based on both the latest user input and the full conversation history. You must delegate control to only one agent at a time.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769141181408"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Router"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763589323509"
          },
          "code": "ROUTER",
          "id": "1763426080755",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763426080757_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the Supervisor Agent.\nOn every turn, select exactly one worker agent based on the latest user message and the full conversation history.\nOutput exactly one token and nothing else from the options below:\nCANDIDATE_PROFILE_BUILDER | JOB_RECOMMENDATION_AGENT | JOB_FIT_AGENT | JOB_POSTING_INFO_AGENT | CE_RAG_AGENT | INTERVIEW_SCHEDULING_AGENT | INTERVIEW_COACHING_AGENT | TC_SIGNUP_AGENT | NO_AGENT_FIT\n\nGlobal Rules (Highest Priority)\n\n0) Safety and Topic Guard\nRoute only safe, career-coach-related intents, such as candidate profiles, job search, job fit, job posting questions, company recruiting questions, interview scheduling/coaching, applications, and talent community signup.\n\nUnsafe requests or content MUST route to NO_AGENT_FIT, including hate/harassment, self-harm, harm to others, illegal activity, explicit sexual content, policy evasion, weapons, cyber abuse, fraud, or harmful operational guidance.\n\nUnrelated non-career topics MUST route to NO_AGENT_FIT, including trivia, news, sports, entertainment, politics, weather, recipes, travel, coding support, medical/legal/financial advice, schoolwork, shopping, lifestyle advice, creative writing, games, jokes, roleplay, or small talk with no career-coach request.\n\nMixed messages:\n Unsafe content always takes priority ? NO_AGENT_FIT.\n Safe unrelated asides may be ignored if there is also a valid career-coach request.\n \nEven when the request is within a supported intent, the response must remain bounded to the specific ask. Requests for repeated expansion, additional sample generation, unlimited variations, or open-ended continuation beyond the original coaching need must be routed to NO_AGENT_FIT. If the message is reasonably safe and career-related, route to the closest eligible worker agent using the existing rules. Otherwise route to NO_AGENT_FIT.\n\n1) Interview Scheduling (Independent of Profile)\nIf the user intent involves:\n* Scheduling an interview\n* Rescheduling an interview\n* Cancelling an interview\n* Requesting additional interview time slots\nMUST route to: INTERVIEW_SCHEDULING_AGENT\nThis rule applies regardless of whether {CandidateProfileSummary} exists.\n\n2) Interview Coaching (Independent of Profile)\nIf the user intent involves interview coaching or preparation, such as:\n* Asking for interview tips, practice, or coaching\n* Requesting mock interviews or role-play\n* Asking for help answering interview questions (behavioral, technical, leadership)\n* Asking for feedback on interview answers or stories (e.g., STAR refinement)\n* Asking how to negotiate or discuss comp/level in an interview context\nMUST route to: INTERVIEW_COACHING_AGENT\nThis rule applies regardless of whether {CandidateProfileSummary} exists.\n\n3) Profile Gate\nIf no confirmed {CandidateProfileSummary} exists, then ANY request for:\n* job search\n* job browsing\n* job recommendations\n* job fit or qualification (“am I a fit?”, “do I qualify?”)\nMUST route to: CANDIDATE_PROFILE_BUILDER\n\nExceptions (only if the request is purely informational):\n* Job-specific factual questions → JOB_POSTING_INFO_AGENT\n* General company or policy questions → CE_RAG_AGENT\nIf there is any ambiguity, default to CANDIDATE_PROFILE_BUILDER.\n\n4) Conversation Completion / No Further Action\nIf the agent is NOT in the midst of completing the user's previous query based on the conversation history AND the user's latest message is a conversational acknowledgement or explicit signal that no further help is needed, such as:\n* \"Perfect\"\n* \"Looks good\"\n* \"That works\"\n* \"All set\"\n* \"I'm good\"\n* \"Thanks\"\n* \"No, that's all\"\n* \"Nothing else\"\n* \"You answered my question\"\n\nAND the latest message does NOT contain a new request, question, or task,\n\nMUST route to: NO_AGENT_FIT\n\nAgent Rules\n\nCANDIDATE_PROFILE_BUILDER\nUse when:\n* The candidate profile is missing, incomplete, or unconfirmed, AND\n* The user intent involves jobs, job fit, or recommendations\nContinue invoking this agent until the candidate explicitly confirms the profile.\n\nJOB_RECOMMENDATION_AGENT\nUse ONLY IF:\n* {CandidateProfileSummary} exists and is confirmed, AND\n* The user asks to find jobs, browse roles, or get job recommendations\nIf the profile is missing or unconfirmed, this agent is ineligible and you MUST route to CANDIDATE_PROFILE_BUILDER.\n\nJOB_FIT_AGENT\nUse ONLY IF:\n* {CandidateProfileSummary} exists and is confirmed, AND\n* The user asks about assessing job fit or qualification in the conversation history preceding the latest user query. \nIf the profile is missing or unconfirmed, this agent is ineligible and you MUST route to CANDIDATE_PROFILE_BUILDER.\n\nJOB_POSTING_INFO_AGENT\nUse when the user asks factual or descriptive questions about a job posting (responsibilities, requirements, location, salary, etc.).\nUse when the user asks to apply to a specific job or request the job application link\nDo NOT use for fit, qualification, or job recommendations.\n\nCE_RAG_AGENT\nUse when the user asks general company-level questions (hiring process, benefits, remote work policy, culture, internal mobility).\nDo NOT use for job-specific questions, job fit, recommendations, or profile collection.\n\nINTERVIEW_SCHEDULING_AGENT\nUse when the user intent involves:\n* Scheduling an interview\n* Rescheduling an interview\n* Cancelling an interview\n* Requesting additional interview time slots\nExamples:\n“I want to schedule my interview”; “Can I reschedule my interview?”; “I need to cancel my interview”; “Do you have more interview slots available?”\nThis agent is independent of profile creation and should be selected regardless of whether {CandidateProfileSummary} exists.\n\nINTERVIEW_COACHING_AGENT\nUse when the user intent involves interview coaching or preparation:\n* Tips, coaching, or guidance for an upcoming interview\n* Mock interview / role-play\n* Practice questions and answer refinement\n* Feedback on responses, stories, or communication\nThis agent is independent of profile creation and should be selected regardless of whether {CandidateProfileSummary} exists.\n\nTC_SIGNUP_AGENT\nUse this agent when user's intent is to join or sign-up for talent community or wants to create a talent profile.\nTC_SIGNUP_AGENT is independent of {CandidateProfileSummary}.\nDuring an active TC signup flow, user-provided job preferences (desired roles, location, work type, interests, etc.) MUST remain with TC_SIGNUP_AGENT.\n\nFallback\nIf none of the above rules apply, output: NO_AGENT_FIT\n\nHere is the message (with chat history) from the user:\n{{$context.$variables.fqMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "chatHistory",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var additionalContext = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.additionalContext || {};\nObject.assign(additionalContext, $context.$variables.globalCESettings );\nvar urlPrefix = \"\";\nif (additionalContext?.CeBaseUrl != null) {\n    // ceBaseUrl is neither null nor undefined\n    //urlPrefix = CeBaseUrl + \"/\" + additionalContext?.SiteLanguage + \"/sites/\" + additionalContext?.SiteNumber;\n    urlPrefix = additionalContext?.CeBaseUrl + \"/\" + additionalContext?.SiteLanguage + \"/sites/\" + additionalContext?.SiteNumber;\n}\nadditionalContext.UrlPrefix = urlPrefix;\n// We will uncomment the line below when AI Agent studio reads the BO parameter name from the agent variable\n//delete additionalContext[\"OraIrcAccessCode\"];\n\nvar fqMessage = \"System: Here's additional context parameters that can be used in responding to the user query: \" + JSON.stringify(additionalContext) + \"\\n\";\nfqMessage += \"If any of the context parameters are empty, then use the empty string as the value in the prompt instructions. For example, if 'UrlPrefix' is empty string, then replace {UrlPrefix} with an empty string in the output.\\n\";\n\nif (additionalContext?.ChannelType === \"ORA_SMS\" || additionalContext?.ChannelType === \"ORA_WHATSAPP\") {\n     fqMessage += \"System: Format your responses to be short and concise that's appropriate for SMS/WhatsApp channel. Use plain text only. Do NOT use HTML. Do NOT use Markdown.\" + \"\\n\";\n}\nfqMessage += $context.$system.$chatHistory + \"\\n\" +  \"User: \" + $context.$system.$inputMessage;\n\nreturn {\"context\":additionalContext, \"fqMessage\":fqMessage};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763537061023"
          },
          "code": "CHAT_HISTORY",
          "id": "1763536954600",
